@coalition_people
title: Coalition and People

# Sources: Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions, ch. 5,
# pp. 249–267; adviser-specific boundaries are recorded under
# docs/research/people/.

= Coalition and People

[? if front_formed = 0: The opposition presently consists of separate
constitutional politicians, the
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!},
newspapers, and personal networks. They cooperate on particular questions
without sharing a formal coalition. ?]
[? if front_formed = 0:
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mohammad Mossadegh{!</span>!} supplies
constitutional coordination, while
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Allahyar Saleh{!</span>!}
connects the work to the organized
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}. ?]

[? if front_formed = 1: The
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!}
joined constitutionalists, the
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}, the
{!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!},
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}independent nationalists{!</span>!},
and religious and bazaar networks without turning
them into one homogeneous party. ?]

[? if front_formed = 1:
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mohammad Mossadegh{!</span>!} served as
its central constitutional coordinator.
{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Hossein Fatemi{!</span>!}
worked through journalism and public advocacy;
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Allahyar Saleh{!</span>!}
through the {!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!};
and {!<span class="term term-makki">!}Hossein Makki{!</span>!} through the
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} and the oil
campaign. {!<span class="term term-religious">!}Ayatollah Abol-Qasem
Kashani{!</span>!} remained an independent ally with his own following. ?]
[? if advisor_maleki_available = 1:
{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Khalil
Maleki{!</span>!} is available through the social-democratic organizational
current. ?]

Further reading:
{!<a href="timeline.html#parties-factions-and-political-networks">!}Parties,
factions, and political networks{!</a>!}; Fakhreddin Azimi,
*Iran: The Crisis of Democracy*, chapter 5, pp. 250–267.

